# Built application files / Gradle
*.apk
*.aar
*.ap_
*.aab
.gradle/
build/
captures/

# …except the ONE checked-in AAR, which is a DEPENDENCY rather than a build output.
#
# `app/libs/llama-android-*.aar` is llama.cpp's Android library, built from source and committed on
# purpose — app/libs/README.md is the whole argument for why — and app/build.gradle.kts consumes it as
# a local file dependency. The blanket `*.aar` rule above is about build output; without this exception
# it silently swallows the app's inference engine, and a fresh clone or a CI checkout then fails with a
# missing-file error that points at Gradle instead of at this line.
!app/libs/*.aar

# Local config — points at your machine's Android SDK; never commit.
local.properties

# Android Studio / IntelliJ
*.iml
.idea/
.DS_Store

# Keystores / signing
*.jks
*.keystore

# NDK
.cxx/
